Binaries/
Build/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
PackagedBuilds/

# Binary assets not tracked via Git LFS
Content/Collections/
Content/Developers/
Content/*.uasset
# Mesh/skeleton/anim sources — pulled from engine plugins, not committed.
# (Recursive: a bare Content/*.uasset above only matches Content/'s direct
# children, so this leaked into git+LFS once before — see commit history.)
#
# Written as /** rather than a bare directory on purpose: an excluded DIRECTORY
# is never descended into, so any !negation inside it is dead. Excluding the
# CONTENTS keeps the directory traversable and lets the exceptions below work.
Content/Characters/**
# ...EXCEPT the handful of project-authored assets the game cannot run without.
# Everything above is re-derivable from the engine's MoverExamples plugin; these
# are not, and CI has no other source for them. Without them an Android build
# silently ships a game whose players neither animate nor render correctly:
#   - ABP_VolleyballPlayer is the Animation Blueprint SetupMesh() loads by path.
#     When the load fails the code falls back to the raw anim instance, which has
#     no AnimGraph — so nothing blends and none of the IK runs. That is the
#     "arms and legs don't move at all" report from the Play build.
#   - IK_Mannequin is the IK Rig whose goals that AnimGraph drives.
#   - SKM_Manny_Simple + M_Mannequin + MI_Manny_0*_New + the Manny textures are
#     the BODY. SetupMesh() prefers this mesh and falls back to the engine's
#     MoverExamples copy, which renders as a pure-black silhouette on Android
#     (measured torso (4,4,4) in *unlit* viewmode, where lighting is removed
#     entirely, against sand at (170,159,131) — so a material problem, not the
#     older lighting bug). The Aug 15 Play build had all 137 of these files
#     tracked and its textures rendered correctly; the Aug 23 purge dropped it
#     to 0 and every Play build since has shipped black players. This is the
#     set that difference comes down to.
#
# These are tracked as PLAIN GIT BLOBS, never LFS (see .gitattributes): LFS
# bandwidth is billed per clone and CI clones on every run, which is what
# exhausted the budget and triggered the purge in the first place. ~45MB total
# against the ~126MB full Mannequins library, most of which stays ignored.
!Content/Characters/Mannequin/
!Content/Characters/Mannequin/**
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Rigs/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Meshes/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Meshes/SKM_Manny_Simple.uasset
# The SKELETON the mesh above binds to. SKM_Manny_Simple.uasset references
# /Game/Characters/Mannequins/Meshes/SK_Mannequin, which is a DIFFERENT asset
# from the /MoverExamples one the Anim BP was authored against — so shipping
# the mesh without this file means the skeleton it names is simply absent from
# a fresh checkout. Only 188K, unlike the 16MB meshes either side of it.
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Meshes/SK_Mannequin.uasset
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Materials/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Materials/M_Mannequin.uasset
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Materials/Functions/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Materials/Functions/**
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Materials/Manny/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Materials/Manny/MI_Manny_0*_New.uasset
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Textures/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Textures/Manny/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Textures/Manny/**
# M_Mannequin samples this alongside the three Manny maps, and MI_Manny_02_New
# references it too — it is one of the base material's five TextureSamples, not
# decoration. Without it a fresh checkout cooks the body material with a
# missing texture. 60K.
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Textures/Shared/
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Textures/Shared/T_UE_Logo_M.uasset
!Content/Characters/Mannequins/Rigs/IK_Mannequin.uasset
# Level maps — CourtLevel.umap is tracked, others are not
Content/*.umap
!Content/CourtLevel.umap

# IDE and compiler artifacts
*.VC.db
*.opensdf
*.opendb
*.sdf
*.suo
*.sln
*.xcworkspace
*.xcodeproj
Config/DefaultEditor.ini
Script/Binds.Cache*

# Android signing material — never committed. NOTE: Config/Android/AndroidEngine.ini
# itself IS tracked (it also carries the mobile SkyAtmosphere override from
# c4b3094) — CI appends the signing block to it rather than overwriting it.
# (Build/ above already covers Build/Android/*.keystore; these are belt-and-suspenders.)
*.keystore
*.jks

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
